msgid "Welcome to the Team & Instructions"
msgstr "チームへようこそ & ご案内"

msgid ""
"Hello, new employee!\n"
"\n"
"Welcome to your first day at our little sushi place. I’m currently on vacation, so I'm sorry I couldn’t be there to welcome you for your first day, but I have faith you'll do great!\n"
"\n"
"As you know from my prior briefings, our operating hours are 9am to 5pm, and arriving an hour early for prep is essential.\n"
"\n"
"Today should be relatively slow considering how new this restaurant is, so you should have some time to figure things out. Additionally, we're operating on a limited menu for now and I'll slowly be introducing new items.\n"
"\n"
"Your main goal is to keep our customers happy by preparing their orders and placing them on the kaiten (that's the sushi belt). You'll see orders pop up from the customers at the counter. Just prepare the requested items, place them on a plate, and send them on their way down the belt.\n"
"\n"
"Time is of the essence! If an order takes too long, the customer will get upset, and our reputation will take a hit. If our reputation drops to zero, we'll have to close our doors for good, and neither of us wants that.\n"
"\n"
"To stay ahead of the game, keep an eye on what customers are ordering. If you notice a particular dish is popular, you can pre-make a few and have them circling on the belt. That way, some customers can grab what they want without having to wait. Happy customers are the key to our success!\n"
"\n"
"I’ll be in touch later in the week with some more tips. For now, just do your best! If you need help on how to make items, there's an index of the recipes you need to know on the computer system.\n"
"\n"
"Best,\n"
"Your Boss"
msgstr ""
"新人さん、こんにちは！\n"
"\n"
"うちの小さな寿司屋での初日へようこそ。私は現在休暇中のため初日に直接迎えられず申し訳ないですが、あなたならきっとうまくやれると信じています。\n"
"\n"
"事前の説明で聞いている通り、営業時間は午前9時から午後5時までで、準備のために1時間前に来ることが必須です。\n"
"\n"
"この店はまだ新しいので、今日は比較的ゆっくりだと思います。落ち着いて仕事の流れをつかんでください。メニューは当面絞っていますが、徐々に新しい品目を追加していきます。\n"
"\n"
"あなたの主な仕事は、お客様を喜ばせることです。注文を作って回転（寿司ベルト）に乗せてください。カウンターのお客様の注文が画面に表示されます。表示された通りに料理を用意して皿に乗せ、ベルトに流してください。\n"
"\n"
"時間が勝負です。注文に時間がかかるとお客様は不満を持ち、店の評判が下がります。評判がゼロになると店を閉めなければならなくなります。それは誰も望んでいません。\n"
"\n"
"先手を打つために、お客様の注文を常にチェックしてください。特に人気のある料理があれば、いくつかあらかじめ作ってベルトに回しておけます。そうすれば、待たずに取れるお客様も増えます。お客様が喜んでくれることが成功の鍵です。\n"
"\n"
"今週後半にまたいくつかコツを連絡します。まずは、がんばってください！料理の作り方がわからないときは、コンピュータのシステムに覚えるべきレシピの索引があります。\n"
"\n"
"よろしく、\n"
"店長"

msgid "Great Work on Day 1!"
msgstr "初日は素晴らしい仕事でした！"

msgid ""
"Hey there,\n"
"\n"
"[reputation=high]\n"
"I just checked the daily report and I have to say, I'm impressed! The place is still standing, and our reputation is looking solid. Thank you.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=medium]\n"
"I just saw the report for the re-opening. A solid performance for your first day, especially since you were on your own. Good work keeping things running.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=low]\n"
"I just looked over the report. Today was a bit of a rocky start, and it looks like a few customers left unhappy. Re-openings are always tough, and it was your first day alone, so don't get too discouraged.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"\n"
"When you're finished tidying up and are ready to call it a night, just head on out the front door; the system will lock up automatically behind you. Feel free to take as much time as you need to prep for tomorrow or rearrange things to your liking.\n"
"\n"
"Speaking of which, don't feel like you have to do everything by hand. I've authorized you to use the day's earnings to invest back into the kitchen. If a task is getting tedious, buy a machine to help out! Working smart is just as important as working hard. In the back corner of the kitchen, there are all the tools you'll need to re-arrange things to your liking or to create a more efficient layout, too. A good flow can make all the difference when things get busy.\n"
"\n"
"Now, for tomorrow: we're bringing back our simple combination dishes. This means you'll start getting orders for things that require multiple ingredients. It's simple, really: to prepare a full dish, just place all of its required ingredients on a plate at the same time and combine them. It's all about good presentation!\n"
"\n"
"[reputation=high]\n"
"Get some rest. You've earned it. Based on today, I know you'll handle tomorrow just fine.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=medium]\n"
"Get some rest tonight. Tomorrow will be a new challenge, but I think you're getting the hang of it.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=low]\n"
"Make sure you read the rest of this email carefully—the tools I'm giving you access to should help a lot. Let's aim for a much smoother day tomorrow. I know you can turn this around.\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"\n"
"Best,\n"
"Your Boss"
msgstr ""
"こんにちは、\n"
"\n"
"[reputation=high]\n"
"日次レポートを確認したところ、感心しました！店は無事で、評判も安定しています。ありがとう。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=medium]\n"
"再開後のレポートを見ました。初日としてはしっかりした仕事ぶりでした、特に一人でやっていたことを考えると。運営を維持してくれてよくやった。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=low]\n"
"レポートを確認しました。今日は少し出だしがつまずき、不満を残して帰ったお客さんが何人かいたようです。再開はいつも難しいし、初めて一人でやる日だったので、あまり落ち込まないでください。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"\n"
"片付けが終わって休みたいときは、そのまま正面の扉から出てください。システムが自動で施錠します。明日の準備や配置替えは、必要なだけ時間をかけて構いません。\n"
"\n"
"ところで、全部手作業でやらなきゃいけないと思わないでください。今日の売上を厨房への投資に使って構わないと許可しています。単調な作業があれば、補助用の機械を買ってください！頭を使って効率的に働くことは、がむしゃらに働くことと同じくらい重要です。厨房の奥の隅には、好きなように配置を変えたり、より効率的なレイアウトを作ったりするための道具が揃っています。忙しくなると、動線の良し悪しが大きな差になります。\n"
"\n"
"さて、明日のことですが：簡単な組み合わせ料理を復活させます。これは複数の材料を必要とする注文が入るということです。やり方は簡単です：一皿にその料理に必要な材料をすべて同時に載せて組み合わせれば、完成です。盛り付けの見栄えも大事ですよ！\n"
"\n"
"[reputation=high]\n"
"ゆっくり休んでください。よく頑張りました。今日の様子なら、明日もうまくやれると信じています。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=medium]\n"
"今夜は休んでください。明日はまた新しい挑戦ですが、コツを掴んできていると思います。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"[reputation=low]\n"
"このメールの残りの部分を注意深く読んでください—使えるようにした道具はきっと助けになります。明日はもっとスムーズな一日にしましょう。必ず挽回できると信じています。\n"
"[/reputation]\n"
"\n"
"よろしくお願いします、\n"
"上司より"

